        "id": 5633
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-07T20:35:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about like this, with a static_cast?\n\nI think I prefer x/y/z/w to walk the hi\u0027s/lo\u0027s. I think it makes it more explicit which part of the vector register they are coming from.\n\nI think operator[] should also walk the hi\u0027s/lo\u0027s as implemented. It will hopefully compile away when the index is compile-time constant, and when not, the calling code ought to figure out exactly which part of the vector register it belongs in, rather than trying to index memory.",
